{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>It shall be washed in a holy place.</b> Scripture has already taught us above that this refers to the court of the Tent of Meeting, from what it said in the section of the meal-offering: ״מצות תאכל במקום קדוש בחצר אהל מועד״ — 'it shall be eaten as unleavened cakes in a holy place, in the court of the Tent of Meeting' — and its counterpart in the Temple is the courtyard (העזרה)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:23:31.659838353Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}